keel (0.15.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * inspect reads overlays.wireguard from the machine. The WireGuard
    overlay owns no unit in its manifest, since its interface is the
    spec's, so inspect looked only at the spec the installer emitted and
    reported "not inferred" on a Core with wg0 up and wg-quick@wg0
    enabled (screenshots 047 and 057 of step 8). It is now read the way
    apply leaves it: enabled when wg-quick@<iface> of the
    /etc/wireguard/<iface>.conf is enabled and, on the live system, the
    interface is up; disabled when neither; not inferred, naming both,
    when they disagree (a change waiting for its confirmation, or an
    interface that went down). The emitted spec still answers when there
    is no WireGuard file.

