keel (0.8.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * spec apply --system converges tls.acme on a running machine. With
    enabled true it writes the domains and, on the live system, runs
    confconsole's dehydrated-wrapper, only when the certificate in use is
    self-signed, does not cover a domain or is within 30 days of its end,
    decided from the certificate as inspect reads it. With enabled false,
    stated, over a certificate a CA issued, it goes back to a self-signed
    one, disables the renewal job and restarts the services that read it.
    Third field of keel#35.
  * tls.acme.agree_tos: registering a Let's Encrypt account accepts its
    terms of service, and apply does so only when the spec says true; a
    machine with an account already needs no consent. diff never compares
    the field. dns-01 is refused: the spec has no provider credentials.
  * apply without the system phase warns that tls.acme waits for it, and
    no longer that certificates are not requested at all.
  * --defer-certificate writes tls.acme and requests nothing; the
    10keel-system hook passes it, since DNS rarely points at a machine
    still at its first boot and a cloned image would spend Let's
    Encrypt's failed validation limit on every copy.
  * An account counts only for the CA the dehydrated config names, at the
    directory dehydrated 0.7.2 derives from it; the old v01 account is
    reused for Let's Encrypt as dehydrated does. Giving the certificate
    back restarts only the units the machine has.

