keel (0.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * spec apply --system renames a running machine to instance.hostname:
    /etc/hostname, the old name as a whole token or first label in
    /etc/hosts, /etc/mailname and postfix's main.cf, then hostnamectl and
    a reload of postfix if it runs. Narrower than 09hostname's sed, which
    also rewrote the name inside other words. The fqdn step plans on the
    renamed /etc/hosts, so the two compose into one file. The self-signed
    certificate is not remade; the run says how. Second field of keel#35.
  * In postfix's main.cf only the values of myhostname and mydestination
    are renamed, so a host called mail, smtp or relay cannot rewrite
    $mail_name or smtpd_relay_restrictions; an underscore is part of a
    name everywhere. A trailing dot is the same name, as diff reads it.
    On the live system a kernel name that a failed hostnamectl left
    behind is set again on the next run.
  * The /etc/hosts step says when the fqdn's first label is not the
    hostname.

